; lane INSTALL -- the install metadata, checked from outside (plan E1; docs/research/2026-10-18-slices/
; README.md §9, ruling 4: names first, no release).
;   check_install.sh  installs every package into a scratch prefix with `dune install`, then builds
;                     a copy of consumer/ outside ocaml/ against that prefix alone: it links the
;                     installed kit, checks and runs one program, and the installed `eff` answers
;                     the same. Red control: the copy cannot name a test library. Its header holds
;                     the behaviours I1-I4.
; consumer/ is the outside project's source. The workspace never builds it: it is data here.

(data_only_dirs consumer)

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (sandbox none)
  (alias_rec %{workspace_root}/install)
  (source_tree consumer)
  installed.expected
  check_install.sh)
 (action
  (run bash %{dep:check_install.sh} %{workspace_root} consumer installed.expected)))
